  steps:
    1. Pick n_largest in [1,3], n_distractor in [0,3], total 2-5
    2. Pick max_area in [3,9]; assign each distractor an area in [2, max_area-1]
    3. Assign distinct non-zero colors to all objects
    4. For each object, generate a random 4-connected blob of its area
    5. Place objects on 10x10 grid with bg=0, ensuring no 8-connected overlap and each object fully inside bounds
    6. Ensure largest objects have distinct bbox left-column values
    7. Verify placement leaves enough room (retry placement if needed)
